# Milestone: v0.9.4 (visit; original draft M3)
# Covers: destroying a Realm cancels all periodics/watchers registered in
#         that Realm; pending bodies do not fire after destruction.
#
# blocked: no driver verb frees a realm.  The action under test is
#          urbi_realm_free, a C entry with no urbiscript surface; the host
#          driver can create and select realms (`## host: realm <name>`)
#          but has no verb for tearing one down.  Adding it is the whole
#          activation.
#
# Everything below this line predates the re-foundation: it names
# tasks and entry points that no longer exist, and its account of
# what stands in the way has been superseded by the `blocked:` line
# above, which was probed against this branch.  Kept for the
# original urbiscript it carries.
#
# Status at v0.9.4: SKIPPED — no urbiscript surface for the action.
#
# urbi_realm_destroy is a C-API entry only.  A urbiscript chunk running
# inside realm R cannot legally destroy R (would yank the rug out from
# under itself).  The chk runner (tests/integration/run_chk.sh) drives one
# REPL session against build/host/urbi and does not provide a C host-
# driver hook to instantiate or destroy realms out-of-band.
#
# Where the two halves stand at the re-foundation:
#   - the TIMER half is covered in C by
#     tests/rt/test_sched.c::freeing_a_realm_drops_its_timers, which arms a
#     periodic in a second realm, frees the realm, and asserts the heap is
#     empty and the VM quiescent.
#   - the WATCHER half has no C-level case today.  urealm_free calls
#     uwatch_realm_dropped (src/rt/urealm.c), which disarms every watcher
#     whose realm is the one going away; nothing asserts it.
#
# The C entry point is urbi_realm_free, not the urbi_realm_destroy this
# header was written against -- that name went with the old core.
#
# To activate this fixture a host-driver tunable would have to be added to
# the chk runner (parallels tests/chk/chunk_lifecycle/realm_isolation.chk —
# both fixtures need T39 chk-runner-host-driver-extension to land).  Until
# then this file stays as a comment-only stub documenting the gap.
#
# Urbyscript sketch (pseudo, activate when T39 + host driver land):
#   [host: create realm R, drive script in R]
#   var called = 0
#   every (1ms) Realm.called = Realm.called + 1
#   [host: urbi_realm_destroy(R)]
#   [host: drive urbi_step a few times; assert no further increment]
